.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt SPACECENTRICITY 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm spacecentricity
.Nd overview of the Spacecentricity project utilities and QMK firmware workflow
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
refers to the Spacecentricity project: a maximalist QMK keymap
implementation, together with the collection of POSIX-compliant shell
utilities used to build and maintain it.
.Pp
The project utilities live in
.Pa scripts/
and provide a small command suite for installing and removing the
keymap, installing project documentation, maintaining license headers,
and building, testing, or flashing the firmware.
.Pp
This page gives an overview of how the utilities relate to one
another. Each utility is documented in full on its own manual page.
.Sh UTILITIES
.Bl -tag -width "license_headers.sh"
.It Xr install.sh 1
Create a symbolic link from the QMK keymap directory to the
Spacecentricity keymap and ask the user to install the optional manual
pages via
.Xr install_man.sh 1 .
.It Xr uninstall.sh 1
Remove the Spacecentricity keymap symlink and any project manual
pages installed by
.Xr install_man.sh 1 .
.It Xr install_man.sh 1
Install or remove the project's manual pages.
.It Xr license_headers.sh 1
Add or remove copyright and license headers on project source files.
.It Xr build.sh 1
Build, flash, lint, clean, check status, or open the QMK debug
console for the Spacecentricity keymap.
.El
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
The following options are supported across the project utilities:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show a help message and exit.
.It Fl -n , Fl -no-banner , Fl -skip-banner
Suppress the ASCII art banner on output.
.El
.Pp
The banner may also be suppressed persistently, without passing a
flag, by setting the
.Ev SPACECENTRICITY_BANNER
environment variable to
.Sq false
or
.Sq 0 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The following environment variables are supported across the project utilities:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev QMK_PATH
Path to your QMK firmware checkout.
Defaults to
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
.It Ev SPACECENTRICITY_BANNER
Set to
.Sq false
or
.Sq 0
to suppress the ASCII art banner by default, without needing
.Fl -no-banner
on every invocation.
.El
.Sh QMK INTEGRATION
The project targets the
.Qq inland/mk47
keyboard and integrates with a local QMK firmware checkout.
.Pp
By default, the QMK checkout is expected to be at
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
This location may be overridden with the
.Ev QMK_PATH
environment variable, accepted by every utility that touches the QMK
tree.
.Pp
The keymap is exposed to QMK through a symbolic link rather than by
copying project files into the QMK source tree. This keeps the
working copy in the project repository while QMK builds from its
expected keymap path.
.Sh WORKFLOW
A typical project workflow:
.Bl -enum
.It
Link the keymap into the QMK checkout:
.Pp
.Dl install.sh
.It
Install the project manual pages:
.Pp
.Dl install_man.sh
.It
Build, lint, check status, or flash the firmware as needed:
.Pp
.Dl build.sh -f
.It
Maintain source-file license headers when adding or editing files:
.Pp
.Dl license_headers.sh
.It
Remove the QMK integration and installed manual pages when done:
.Pp
.Dl uninstall.sh
.El
.Pp
Keep the QMK firmware checkout itself current independently, using
.Xr git 1
inside the QMK tree.
.Sh PROJECT ROOT
The project root provides a convenience stub for the most frequently
used utility. The
.Pa build
stub invokes
.Xr build.sh 1
without requiring the script's path to be specified explicitly.
.Pp
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./build
\&./build -f
\&./build --check
.Ed
.Sh DOCUMENTATION
Project manual pages are maintained in
.Pa docs/man/
using the
.Xr mdoc 7
format, and may be installed with
.Xr install_man.sh 1
or removed as part of
.Xr uninstall.sh 1 .
.Pp
The individual pages provide detailed command reference for each
utility; this manual page serves as the overview tying them together.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "scripts/license_headers.sh"
.It Pa scripts/
Project shell utilities.
.It Pa docs/man/
Project manual pages, in
.Xr mdoc 7
source format.
.It Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware
Default QMK firmware checkout location.
.El
